{"content_hash": "e2a016f5c988dd35", "version_id": 246, "article_id": 25, "level_code": "ja_n5", "lang": "ja", "level": 1, "level_label": "N5 初級", "title": "アメリカとレバノン、シリアの将軍を守る", "title_zh": "美国和黎巴嫩在保护一名叙利亚将军", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c81dldewl5gwo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/6350/live/ef6a77a0-c1a6-11f1-a64c-550be9e3c66b.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 358, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "シリアの元将軍がアメリカとレバノンに守られています。BBCが調べました。この将軍は戦争犯罪でほしい人です。", "lead_zh": "一名叙利亚前将军正受到美国和黎巴嫩的保护。BBC进行了调查。这名将军因战争罪被通缉。", "preview": "シリアの元将軍バッサム・アルハッサンは、戦争犯罪でほしい人です。彼はシリアの化学兵器を管理していました。2024年にアサド政権が倒れた後、彼はレバノンにいます。", "preview_zh": "叙利亚前将军巴萨姆·阿尔哈桑是因战争罪被通缉的人。他曾负责管理叙利亚的化学武器。2024年阿萨德政权倒台后，他身处黎巴嫩。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 236, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/audio/25/ja_n5.mp3", "duration": 76.587, "size_bytes": 463248, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 229, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/data/versions/246.json", "paragraphs": ["シリアの元将軍バッサム・アルハッサンは、戦争犯罪でほしい人です。彼はシリアの化学兵器を管理していました。2024年にアサド政権が倒れた後、彼はレバノンにいます。", "BBCとアメリカのNPRが調べました。ハッサンはFBIなどと約束をしました。2012年にアメリカの記者オースティン・タイスが誘拐されました。ハッサンはその情報を出すと言いました。それで、レバノンにいていいと言われました。", "シリアの新しい政府は、ハッサンを裁判にかけたいと言っています。しかし、アメリカはレバノンにいてほしいと言っています。ダマスカスにはできることが少ないです。", "タイスの家族の人は怒っています。「これは戦争犯罪人を助けることです。シリア人は正義を求めています。彼は裁判を受けるべきです」と言いました。", "ハッサンはアメリカからお金をもらっています。しかし、タイスの事件はあまり進んでいません。他のシリアの役人も外国にいます。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["叙利亚前将军巴萨姆·阿尔哈桑是因战争罪被通缉的人。他曾负责管理叙利亚的化学武器。2024年阿萨德政权倒台后，他身处黎巴嫩。", "BBC和美国NPR进行了调查。哈桑与FBI等达成了约定。2012年，美国记者奥斯汀·泰斯被绑架。哈桑表示愿意提供相关情报。因此，他被允许留在黎巴嫩。", "叙利亚新政府表示希望将哈桑送上法庭。但美国希望他留在黎巴嫩。大马士革对此无能为力。", "泰斯的家人非常愤怒。他们说：“这是在帮助战争罪犯。叙利亚人要求正义。他应该接受审判。”", "哈桑从美国获得资金。但泰斯案件进展甚微。其他叙利亚官员也身在国外。"], "body": "シリアの元将軍バッサム・アルハッサンは、戦争犯罪でほしい人です。彼はシリアの化学兵器を管理していました。2024年にアサド政権が倒れた後、彼はレバノンにいます。\n\nBBCとアメリカのNPRが調べました。ハッサンはFBIなどと約束をしました。2012年にアメリカの記者オースティン・タイスが誘拐されました。ハッサンはその情報を出すと言いました。それで、レバノンにいていいと言われました。\n\nシリアの新しい政府は、ハッサンを裁判にかけたいと言っています。しかし、アメリカはレバノンにいてほしいと言っています。ダマスカスにはできることが少ないです。\n\nタイスの家族の人は怒っています。「これは戦争犯罪人を助けることです。シリア人は正義を求めています。彼は裁判を受けるべきです」と言いました。\n\nハッサンはアメリカからお金をもらっています。しかし、タイスの事件はあまり進んでいません。他のシリアの役人も外国にいます。", "body_zh": "叙利亚前将军巴萨姆·阿尔哈桑是因战争罪被通缉的人。他曾负责管理叙利亚的化学武器。2024年阿萨德政权倒台后，他身处黎巴嫩。\n\nBBC和美国NPR进行了调查。哈桑与FBI等达成了约定。2012年，美国记者奥斯汀·泰斯被绑架。哈桑表示愿意提供相关情报。因此，他被允许留在黎巴嫩。\n\n叙利亚新政府表示希望将哈桑送上法庭。但美国希望他留在黎巴嫩。大马士革对此无能为力。\n\n泰斯的家人非常愤怒。他们说：“这是在帮助战争罪犯。叙利亚人要求正义。他应该接受审判。”\n\n哈桑从美国获得资金。但泰斯案件进展甚微。其他叙利亚官员也身在国外。", "text": "シリアの元将軍バッサム・アルハッサンは、戦争犯罪でほしい人です。彼はシリアの化学兵器を管理していました。2024年にアサド政権が倒れた後、彼はレバノンにいます。 BBCとアメリカのNPRが調べました。ハッサンはFBIなどと約束をしました。2012年にアメリカの記者オースティン・タイスが誘拐されました。ハッサンはその情報を出すと言いました。それで、レバノンにいていいと言われました。 シリアの新しい政府は、ハッサンを裁判にかけたいと言っています。しかし、アメリカはレバノンにいてほしいと言っています。ダマスカスにはできることが少ないです。 タイスの家族の人は怒っています。「これは戦争犯罪人を助けることです。シリア人は正義を求めています。彼は裁判を受けるべきです」と言いました。 ハッサンはアメリカからお金をもらっています。しかし、タイスの事件はあまり進んでいません。他のシリアの役人も外国にいます。", "vocab": [{"word": "将軍", "pos": "noun", "zh": "将军", "note": ""}, {"word": "戦争犯罪", "pos": "noun", "zh": "战争罪", "note": ""}, {"word": "守る", "pos": "verb", "zh": "保护", "note": ""}, {"word": "調べる", "pos": "verb", "zh": "调查", "note": ""}, {"word": "誘拐", "pos": "noun", "zh": "绑架", "note": ""}, {"word": "裁判", "pos": "noun", "zh": "审判", "note": ""}, {"word": "情報", "pos": "noun", "zh": "情报", "note": ""}, {"word": "政府", "pos": "noun", "zh": "政府", "note": ""}], "title_original": "US and Lebanon protecting wanted Syrian general, BBC finds", "summary_original": "Bassam al-Hassan, linked to reporter Austin Tice's abduction, is being sheltered in return for information.", "body_original": "US and Lebanon protecting wanted Syrian general, BBC finds\nBy\nSara Obeidat\nand\nJosh Baker\nPublished\n4 hours ago\nA former Syrian general wanted for\ncrimes against humanity\n,\nexternal\nis being bankrolled and protected by the US and Lebanese authorities, a BBC News investigation has found.\nBassam al-Hassan, who oversaw Syria's chemical weapons programme and was a senior adviser to former President Bashar al-Assad, is being harboured in Lebanon following the Assad regime's collapse in 2024.\nAn investigation by the BBC and the US broadcaster NPR has discovered that Hassan has been allowed to remain there under an arrangement involving the FBI, and other US and Lebanese authorities. This is because of his willingness to provide information about the abduction of American journalist Austin Tice in Syria in 2012, as well as additional intelligence, we have been told.\nLast month the BBC revealed Tice's abduction had been a\nplanned operation\n, with Hassan in the chain of command.\nOfficials from two different branches of Syria's new government have told the BBC they want Hassan returned to face trial, but that US authorities want him kept in Lebanon, and they say there is little Damascus can do about this.\nWe asked the FBI, the CIA and Lebanon's General Directorate of General Security to comment on our findings. Only the FBI responded, declining to comment and instead directing us to a past statement that said its focus remained on establishing the facts around the Tice case and securing his return.\nIn response to our findings, Phil Elwood, spokesperson for the Tice family said: \"If what you are saying is true, the fact that our tax dollars are being used to furnish a comfortable life for someone associated with the use of chemical weapons on Syrian civilians, who claims to have had Austin Tice executed, is offensive.\n\"This is nothing less than aiding and abetting the escape of a wanted war criminal. The Syrians deserve justice and he should be returned to stand trial.\"\nWhere is Austin Tice?\nJosh Baker enters a dangerous world of fear, greed and betrayal as he uncovers what happened in one of the biggest missing-person cases of our time - the abduction of Austin Tice.\nListen on Sounds\nSeries Three of I'm Not A Monster Presents\nAs part of a years-long investigation featured in the new\nBBC podcast: Where is Austin Tice?\nthe BBC has reviewed a detailed record of a meeting between Hassan, FBI and CIA representatives, and Lebanese security officials, where Tice's case is discussed.\nIn it, Hassan is offered \"residency\", \"protection\" and help securing his \"living needs\" in return for information, primarily about Tice.\nSources with knowledge of the arrangement confirmed this was the case, and described to us how Hassan receives money from the US authorities through an intermediary, making it harder to trace. Hassan is sanctioned by the US government.\nYet people connected to the Tice investigation say they have seen little evidence it has significantly advanced since Hassan began providing information as part of this agreement. The deal is believed to have been struck in the spring of 2025.\nSources with knowledge of the investigation have expressed concerns that Hassan's arrangement with the US could continue indefinitely, at significant expense but with little gain.\nHassan is not the only Syrian regime official whose connection to the Tice case has seemingly afforded him financial payments or assistance for living abroad.\nOne former regime member said he had received money from the FBI multiple times in exchange for his co-operation on Tice's case. It was \"not in his interest to share all the information all at once,\" he told the BBC, \"in order to be able to drag out how long he can continue to receive payments from them [the US authorities]\".\nAnother former regime member connected to the Tice case claimed he was living in Lebanon under the \"patronage\" of the US authorities, citing this as the reason he could not speak to us about Tice.\nThe BBC spoke to a former senior Lebanese intelligence official who confirmed that Lebanese intelligence does have arrangements with the Americans, and that these types of payments have and do take place when both agencies have overlap in cases, but said he had no knowledge of payments involving the Tice case.\nFollowing the fall of the Assad regime in early December 2024, Hassan is believed to have initially escaped to Iran.\nA Syrian businessman, with strong connections to both the former regime and the Lebanese authorities, told the BBC that negotiations had then taken place - involving the US, Lebanon, and Iran - to bring Hassan to Lebanon.\nThe businessman, who asked to remain anonymous, said Hassan was valuable, not only because of what he is believed to know about Tice, but because of his knowledge of Syria's chemical weapons programme and its military relationship with Iran - secrets that US intelligence was allegedly interested in.\nHassan told US investigators last year that Tice\nhad been executed\non former President Assad's orders, but several people with knowledge of the investigation have questioned the details of his account. Hassan has provided a potential location for Tice's remains, but when the site was searched, nothing was found - according to multiple sources familiar with the dig - casting doubt on the validity of some of Hassan's information.\nThere are questions, however, over how thoroughly the site was searched. Two sources who said they had intimate knowledge of the operation told the BBC that US authorities stopped digging before the search had been completed, possibly because of security concerns.\nWhen the BBC managed to reach Hassan by phone last year to ask for an interview, he directed us to seek permission for him to speak from the FBI and CIA at the US embassy in Beirut.\nOur investigation has found that other Syrian officials connected to the Tice case have also apparently found refuge abroad.\nThey include Mohammad Makhlouf, who reported to Hassan in Syria and was connected to Tice's detention - now believed to be residing in Lebanon. And Sakr Rustom, Hassan's nephew who was involved in Tice's abduction, now believed to be moving between the UAE and Lebanon. When the BBC attempted to speak to Rustom about Tice's case, he said he \"preferred to focus on matters of the future\".\nGhassan Nassour, a former general in Syria's Republican Guard, is said by former members of the National Defence Forces to have presided over the jail Tice was held in, and is believed to be living in the UAE with his family, we have been told.\nRelated topics\nSyria\nUS government\nUnited States\nFBI\nCIA\nSyrian civil war\nBashar al-Assad", "fetched_at": "2026-10-08T09:37:52.374921+00:00", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "シリア", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.537, "sm": 125, "em": 537, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.55, "e": 0.663, "sm": 550, "em": 662, "cs": 3, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "元", "s": 0.675, "e": 0.925, "sm": 675, "em": 925, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "将軍", "s": 0.938, "e": 1.4, "sm": 937, "em": 1400, "cs": 5, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "バッサム", "s": 1.413, "e": 1.95, "sm": 1412, "em": 1950, "cs": 7, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "・", "s": 1.95, "e": 2.163, "sm": 1950, "em": 2162, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "アルハッサン", "s": 2.163, "e": 2.9, "sm": 2162, "em": 2900, "cs": 12, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "は", "s": 2.913, "e": 3.175, "sm": 2912, "em": 3175, "cs": 18, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "、", "s": 3.175, "e": 3.413, "sm": 3175, "em": 3412, "cs": 19, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "戦争", "s": 3.413, "e": 3.9, "sm": 3412, "em": 3900, "cs": 20, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "犯罪", "s": 3.913, "e": 4.362, "sm": 3912, "em": 4362, "cs": 22, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "で", "s": 4.375, "e": 4.45, "sm": 4375, "em": 4450, "cs": 24, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "ほしい", "s": 4.463, "e": 4.838, "sm": 4462, "em": 4837, "cs": 25, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "人", "s": 4.85, "e": 5.075, "sm": 4850, "em": 5074, "cs": 28, "ce": 29, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "です", "s": 5.088, "e": 5.463, "sm": 5087, "e